<title>CHINA: Shanghai grain exchange closes for HK handover.</title>
<headline>Shanghai grain exchange closes for HK handover.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai Cereals and Oils Exchange will close next Monday and Tuesday to celebrate the return of Hong Kong to Chinese rule at midnight on June 30, an exchange official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Trading would resume on Wednesday, he said.</p>
<p>The key November 1997 contract ended at an intraday high of 3,303 yuan ($398) per tonne, rising 15 yuan. It opened at 3,290 yuan and hit a low of 3,286 yuan per tonne.</p>
</text>
